I keep forgetting to ask you this... Is there any way to get qt to throw away events when it gets too many? XWindows, and I think gtk, had a function called "flush" which cleared out the event queue periodically. Currently its possible to hang cranvas, if you click a button too many times, as wt struggles to get through responding to all the events.

